# Theme and Styling Guidelines

## CSS Variables (Single Source of Truth)

All colors are defined as CSS variables in `styles/globals.css`. The current design uses a **dark aesthetic** (`:root`). A `.light` class can be added later for light mode. 

### Color Categories

| Category | Variables | Usage |
|----------|-----------|-------|
| Brand | `--eduhub-brand`, `--eduhub-brand-light`, `--eduhub-brand-dark` | Primary actions, links, highlights |
| Fill | `--eduhub-fill-primary`, `--eduhub-fill-secondary` | Button fills, backgrounds |
| Label | `--eduhub-label-primary`, `--eduhub-label-secondary` | Text colors |
| Border | `--eduhub-border-primary`, `--eduhub-border-secondary` | Borders, dividers |
| Background | `--eduhub-bg-primary`, `--eduhub-bg-secondary`, `--eduhub-bg-modal` | Page/component backgrounds |
| Functional | `--eduhub-success`, `--eduhub-warning`, `--eduhub-error`, `--eduhub-info` | Status indicators |
| Status | `--eduhub-status-confirmed`, `--eduhub-status-invited`, etc. | Enrollment/course status |

## MANDATORY: Use Semantic Colors

### In Tailwind (preferred)

Use semantic class names that reference CSS variables:

```tsx
// Good - semantic names
<div className="bg-fill-primary text-label-primary border-border-primary">
<button className="bg-brand hover:bg-brand-dark text-fill-primary">

// Avoid - hardcoded colors
<div className="bg-white text-gray-900">
<div className="bg-[#00A398]">
```

### In Inline Styles (when necessary)

```tsx
// Good - CSS variables
<div style={{ backgroundColor: 'var(--eduhub-bg-secondary)' }}>

// Avoid - hardcoded
<div style={{ backgroundColor: '#F2F2F2' }}>
```

### In MUI Components

The MUI theme is configured to use brand colors. Use theme-aware props:

```tsx
// Good - uses theme
<Button color="primary">
<Typography color="text.primary">

// Avoid - overriding with hardcoded
<Button sx={{ backgroundColor: '#00A398' }}>
```

## Adding New Colors

1. Add CSS variable to `styles/globals.css` under appropriate category
2. Add Tailwind reference in `tailwind.config.js`
3. If needed for MUI, update `config/theme.ts`

## Legacy Color Migration

Old `edu-*` classes are aliased to CSS variables for backward compatibility:

- `edu-green` → `var(--eduhub-brand)`
- `edu-black` → `var(--eduhub-label-primary)`

When modifying components, prefer migrating to semantic names:

- `bg-edu-green` → `bg-brand`
- `text-edu-black` → `text-label-primary`
